{
  "$comment": [
    "Declared path -> suite map for TEST-004 (forge-ci/ci.yml#518). Read by ci/select-tests.mjs.",
    "suites: every node --test file `npm test` runs (its `pretest` and `test` lists), in exactly one named suite; their union must equal those lists (checked).",
    "unlisted: test files `npm test` does not name but runs because a listed test imports them (main.test.ts imports yank-audit.test.ts, log-utils.test.ts imports target-lifecycle.test.ts, soldr-load-shim.test.ts imports cargo-registry-archive.test.ts). Editing one selects the suites of the tests that import it.",
    "always: a change here selects every suite (tooling/config that decides what the suites do).",
    "ignore: paths that provably cannot change a node test result; they select nothing. Mirrors the gate's TEST_SAFE_EXCLUSIONS.",
    "rules: glob -> suites, evaluated additively. A changed path that matches no rule, no `always` and no `ignore` selects every suite (fail closed).",
    "A changed test file selects the suite that lists it plus the suites of every test that imports it; an added/renamed/deleted test file, or one in no suite and not unlisted, selects everything.",
    "The selector then checks the declared result against the import graph of every test file and fails the run if a suite whose tests import the changed file was not selected (the under-selection guard).",
    "The rules were derived from the measured import graph (node ci/select-tests.mjs graph) and are kept honest by `check`: a synthetic edit to every file any test reads must select that test's suite through these rules alone.",
    "opaque: tests whose string literals are data, not file reads (the selector's own test names fixture paths); the literal-path heuristic skips them, their imports still count."
  ],
